/* holy-symbol-slot-helm.irh -- fixture for tools/check_holy_symbol_slots.sh.
   Bead inc-tf6l: does a god-marked item worn in a non-old slot (the helm) work
   as a holy symbol?

   THE PROBLEM THIS FIXTURE SOLVES. The defect is that Creature::Turn and the
   divine component check search only {SL_READY, SL_WEAPON, SL_AMULET,
   SL_ARMOUR}. To show the fix, an item must be god-marked and worn in a NEW
   slot. No shipped data can do that: the only god-marked gear in lib/ is the
   player's starting `holy symbol` (T_SYMBOL, lib/races.irh) and the shield a
   priest template stamps (T_SHIELD, lib/mon2.irh), and both are active only in
   the four old slots. This fixture adds a HELMET effect whose resource name
   begins with a real god's name, "Aiswin".

   THE MATCH. The two fix sites test a god mark with
   `!strncmp(NAME(it->eID), NAME(godID), strlen(NAME(godID)))`. A priest of
   Aiswin has NAME(godID) == "Aiswin"; this helm's eID resource is named
   "Aiswin Test Helm". NAME() truncates at the first ';' and stops there, so
   the test is strncmp("Aiswin Test Helm", "Aiswin", 6) == 0 -- a god mark by the
   code's own rule. Nothing here changes the code; it only supplies the item
   the shipped data lacks.

   WHY EA_GENERIC. It grants nothing, so the item is a plain helm with an eID
   and no side effects, which is all the mark test reads.

   NOT part of the shipped module: tools/check_holy_symbol_slots.sh copies lib/
   to a scratch directory and appends this file to the END of the copy's
   main.irc for the span of its own run, the same shape
   tools/check_skc6_blast_text.sh uses. Appending is required, never a mid-file
   insert: a v1 save records each resource array's length and each entry's name
   in POSITION order, so a mid-file insert would shift every later resource. No
   tracked lib/ file is ever touched. */

AI_HELM Effect "Aiswin Test Helm" : EA_GENERIC
  { Desc: "A test helm bearing the emblem of Aiswin, for the inc-tf6l holy-symbol
      slot check only. It grants nothing; it exists so a god-marked item can be
      worn in the helmet slot, which no shipped item can do."; }
